:[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/Key.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" & "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hotkey string to normalize"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"platform","children":[{"type":"text","value":"platform?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"mac\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"windows\""},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"linux\""}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The target platform for resolving "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod"},{"type":"text","value":" (defaults to auto-detection)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/Hotkey.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Hotkey"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The normalized hotkey string"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"normalizeHotkey('shift+meta+e', 'mac') // 'Mod+Shift+E'\nnormalizeHotkey('ctrl+a', 'windows') // 'Mod+A'\nnormalizeHotkey('esc') // 'Escape'","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"hotkey","text":"hotkey","level":3},{"id":"platform","text":"platform?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction normalizeHotkey(hotkey, platform?): Hotkey;\n```\n\nDefined in: [parse.ts:205](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/parse.ts#L205)\n\nNormalizes a hotkey string to its canonical form.\n\n- When `Mod` is allowed for the platform (Command on Mac without Control;\n  Control on Windows/Linux without Meta): emits `Mod`, then `Alt`, then `Shift`,\n  then the key (e.g. `Mod+Shift+E`, `Mod+S`).\n- Otherwise: literal modifiers in `Control+Alt+Shift+Meta` order, then the key.\n- Resolves aliases and normalizes key casing (e.g. `esc` → `Escape`, `a` → `A`).\n\n## Parameters\n\n### hotkey\n\n[`Key`](../type-aliases/Key.md) \\| `string` & `object`\n\nThe hotkey string to normalize\n\n### platform?\n\n`\"mac\"` \\| `\"windows\"` \\| `\"linux\"`\n\nThe target platform for resolving `Mod` (defaults to auto-detection)\n\n## Returns\n\n[`Hotkey`](../type-aliases/Hotkey.md)\n\nThe normalized hotkey string\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nnormalizeHotkey('shift+meta+e', 'mac') // 'Mod+Shift+E'\nnormalizeHotkey('ctrl+a', 'windows') // 'Mod+A'\nnormalizeHotkey('esc') // 'Escape'\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: normalizeHotkey\ntitle: normalizeHotkey\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction normalizeHotkey(hotkey, platform?): Hotkey;\n```\n\nDefined in: [parse.ts:205](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/hotkeys/src/parse.ts#L205)\n\nNormalizes a hotkey string to its canonical form.\n\n- When `Mod` is allowed for the platform (Command on Mac without Control;\n  Control on Windows/Linux without Meta): emits `Mod`, then `Alt`, then `Shift`,\n  then the key (e.g. `Mod+Shift+E`, `Mod+S`).\n- Otherwise: literal modifiers in `Control+Alt+Shift+Meta` order, then the key.\n- Resolves aliases and normalizes key casing (e.g. `esc` → `Escape`, `a` → `A`).\n\n## Parameters\n\n### hotkey\n\n[`Key`](../type-aliases/Key.md) \\| `string` & `object`\n\nThe hotkey string to normalize\n\n### platform?\n\n`\"mac\"` \\| `\"windows\"` \\| `\"linux\"`\n\nThe target platform for resolving `Mod` (defaults to auto-detection)\n\n## Returns\n\n[`Hotkey`](../type-aliases/Hotkey.md)\n\nThe normalized hotkey string\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nnormalizeHotkey('shift+meta+e', 'mac') // 'Mod+Shift+E'\nnormalizeHotkey('ctrl+a', 'windows') // 'Mod+A'\nnormalizeHotkey('esc') // 'Escape'\n```\n"}
